{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter and Online Dating"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Finding That Special Someone"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 11}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le11ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Phrasal Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Phrasal verbs consist of a verb and one or more prepositions. They are common, especially in informal spoken English. The meaning of phrasal verbs is often completely different from the meaning of the verb alone.<br/>Phrasal verbs can either be separable or inseparable."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Separable phrasal verbs consist of two parts. They always require an object."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The object of a phrasal verb can go either between the verb and the preposition or after the preposition."}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"underline\">Examples</span>:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I handed in my homework.<br/> I handed my homework in.</span><br/> "}, {"type": "text", "content": " If the object of the sentence is an object pronoun, it must go between the two parts of the phrasal verb. <br> <br><span class=\"underline\">Example</span>:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I handed it in.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some phrasal verbs are inseparable, so the verb must be directly followed by its preposition or adverb. Otherwise, the meaning of the phrasal verb will be incorrect.<br/>Some inseparable phrasal verbs never use an object."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">Examples</span>: <ul><li>get up = get out of bed   <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I get up at seven o'clock every morning.<br/></li> <li>take off = leave the ground <br/>          <span class=\"italic\">The plane took off on time.</span></li> <li>look out = beware! be careful!   <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Look out! That car is going to hit you!</span></li>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to fall out with \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to end a relationship after a disagreement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to look for\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to search for someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to log in\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to access a website by entering a password\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to log out\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to exit a website by removing the password\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to pop up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to appear on another window\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: I've only fallen out with two of the new guys that I've met online. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: You should show me how to log in to that website you mentioned."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Present Perfect Continuous vs Present Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. <br/><br/>You use Present Perfect Continuous tense to describe:<ul><li> a single activity that lasts a long time, and</li><li>  an action that is repeated over a long period of time.</li></ul>These continue up to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about experience. When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I have learned English</span> = I learned English in the past and now I can speak English.<br/> <span class=\"italic\">He has bought a painting</span> = He bought the painting in the past and now he has a painting. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the Present Perfect Continuous tense when a long activity has just stopped."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To emphasize the action, use the continuous form.<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>We've been working really hard for a couple of months.</li> <li>She's been having a hard time.</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "To emphasize the result of the action, use the simple form.<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Have you updated your profile like I asked you to?</li><li> I've met many cool guys that way. </li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Subject</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Have</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Been</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Verb+ing</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" has\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"been\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"   talking on the phone <span class=\\\"strong\\\">for</span> an hour.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" They \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"been \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"working there <span class=\\\"strong\\\">since</span> 2010.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>You use FOR to talk about how long an action has been happening (a week, 2 days, five hours, six years etc.) </li><li>You use SINCE to talk about when the action started (2010, Monday, she was a child)  </li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've been subscribing to this service for a few months now. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " Since last year, I've been using a program that logs you in automatically."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Subject</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">has/have</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">past participle</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"'ve\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"fallen out with two of them.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"has\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"met many guys that way.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pop up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to show up on another window in your computer"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A new message popped up on another window."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use in a conversation about an online profile."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to subscribe"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to register to a service"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've been subscribing to this service for a few months now."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "username"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a name you use on your online profiles"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You need to input your username in order to access the site."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to log in"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to insert a name and password to access a website"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You need to log in with your username and password."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to log out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to exit a website you previously logged in"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Don't forget to log out!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to look for"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to search for something or someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "cont